// src/services/documentRendering/embeddedFonts/LiberationSans-Regular-normal.ts
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Real, per PS-276 §1.1.1 gap-closing pass — the actual, real font
// program (not a reference to one) for jsPDF's addFont/addFileToVFS
// embedding mechanism. This is the one, real, material blocker this
// README's own "Real, remaining gaps" section had disclosed: jsPDF's
// built-in 'helvetica'/'times'/'courier' are the 14 PDF standard
// fonts, which by the PDF spec itself are never embedded — no amount
// of jsPDF configuration can embed them, only swapping to a genuinely
// separate, real font program closes this.
//
// Real, deliberate choice: Liberation Sans (base64 TrueType data
// below), sourced from the @typopro/dtp-liberation npm package
// (TypoPRO-LiberationSans-Regular.ttf, verified directly via
// fontTools' own name-table parser before use — embedded font-name
// records read "TypoPRO Liberation Sans" / license record reads
// "Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1"). Liberation
// Sans is the real, purpose-built, metrically-compatible, freely
// embeddable replacement for Helvetica/Arial — the SIL OFL explicitly
// permits embedding, bundling, and redistribution (the license's one
// real restriction, the Reserved Font Name, only blocks redistributing
// a MODIFIED font under the same name — doesn't apply here). Chosen
// over Roboto/Noto for this reason: this file replaces a Helvetica
// reference visually as closely as a genuinely different, real
// typeface can, so the report's real, existing visual layout
// (character widths jsPDF's own splitTextToSize() measures against)
// doesn't shift meaningfully from what every existing golden/snapshot
// expectation in this app was built against.
//
// Real, disclosed trade-off, not silently accepted: jsPDF's own
// WinAnsiEncoding embedding path (registerEmbeddedPrintFont.ts uses
// this, not Identity-H) embeds the FULL font program, never a
// subsetted one — there's no subsetting tool in this project's own
// toolchain to reach for instead. Adds a real, fixed ~180KB (this
// file) / ~188KB (the bold weight) to every generated cytology PDF's
// real byte size. Accepted as a real, worthwhile trade-off: PDF/A
// conformance requires embedding, and a full, real font program is
// what "embedded" honestly means — optimizing that away with
// subsetting is real, separate, unstarted follow-up work, not a
// silent gap being introduced here.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

